# The image runs the service (app/, requirements.txt) and carries the small text-only
# catalogue tooling the Dockerfile COPYs — the driver, the loader, the verified merchant list.
# Everything below is either build-time-only or large, and none of it is COPYed, but an
# un-ignored file still gets shipped to the daemon as build context on every build.
#
# Without this file the context is ~32 MB today, and ~280 MB after a --browserbase run.

# Generated by build_prebake.py. Committed today so Ani is unblocked; moves to R2 later.
# Stays out of the image: it is an input to load_catalog.py, which reads it from the host.
# ceiling: when prebake/ moves to R2, this line and the .gitignore note both go.
prebake/

# Fetched product pages, ~450 KB each.
.page-cache/

# Catalogue run output: raw pulls, extracted rows, generated SQL and upload scripts.
# Regenerable by definition, and .bulk/ holds a full copy of every catalogue crawled.
.bulk/
.load/

# Build-time and dev-time only.
tests/
samples/
build_prebake.py
probe_page.py
candidates*.json
merchants.example.json
*.md

# NOT ignored, and COPYed by the Dockerfile — see the comment there:
#   bulk_ingest.py, load_catalog.py, verify_merchants.py, merchants.verified.json

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
